PROJECT RISK REGISTER

1. Purpose

This document identifies the main risks that may affect the development and use of the AI-Based Platform for Academic Integrity Verification and Personal Contribution Assessment.

2. Identified Risks

R-1: Incorrect AI Text Classification

Probability: Medium
Impact: High
Mitigation: Evaluate the model using a separate test set and report precision, recall, F1-score, and a confusion matrix.

R-2: Insufficient or Imbalanced Dataset

Probability: Medium
Impact: High
Mitigation: Use suitable labelled data, check class balance, and document dataset limitations.

R-3: Incomplete Contribution Assessment

Probability: High
Impact: High
Mitigation: Use multiple indicators, explain their limitations, and avoid treating activity data as a definitive measure of individual contribution.

R-4: Limited Access to External Data

Probability: Medium
Impact: Medium
Mitigation: Use authorized access, test integrations early, and handle unavailable data appropriately.

R-5: Unauthorized Access to Personal or Academic Data

Probability: Low to Medium
Impact: High
Mitigation: Implement access controls, obtain appropriate authorization, and store only the data necessary for system operation.

R-6: Project Delays

Probability: Medium
Impact: High
Mitigation: Prioritize core features, assign responsibilities clearly, and review progress regularly in YouTrack.

R-7: Poor System Performance

Probability: Medium
Impact: Medium
Mitigation: Measure response times during testing and optimize components when necessary.

3. Risk Monitoring

The team will review risks throughout development and update this register when new issues arise or existing risks change.

4. Ethical Considerations

AI classification results are estimates and may be incorrect. Contribution indicators may be incomplete or misleading. The platform will support human review and will not make automatic disciplinary decisions.

5. Current Status

This register describes potential risks and planned mitigation measures. The probability and impact of each risk will be reviewed as implementation and testing progress.
